From e299d67ae84d6634e4725888408adbf26a5051f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:51:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: vop2: Mask POST_BUF_EMPTY in the RK3576 handler

rk3576_vp_isr() clears POST_BUF_EMPTY and leaves it enabled, so on
RK3576 a persistent underflow raises the interrupt again as soon as it
is cleared and turns into an interrupt storm.

Disable the interrupt when it fires. vop2_crtc_atomic_flush() enables
it again with the next committed configuration.

Fixes: 944757a4cba6 ("drm/rockchip: vop2: Add support for rk3576")
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_vop2.c
@@ -2195,6 +2195,7 @@ static irqreturn_t rk3576_vp_isr(int irq
 	}
 
 	if (irqs & VP_INT_POST_BUF_EMPTY) {
+		vop2_crtc_disable_irq(vp, VP_INT_POST_BUF_EMPTY);
 		drm_err_ratelimited(vop2->drm, "POST_BUF_EMPTY irq err at vp%d\n", vp->id);
 		ret = IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
